COACH: You're close, Jonathan! Let me clarify it a little.

next() is actually what tells Express to continue to the next step — meaning if the user passes both checks (logged in and has the right role), next() hands control over to the actual route handler, like showEditProjectForm.

If you forgot to call next(), the request would just hang forever — the user's browser would keep waiting for a response that never comes, even though they had the correct role and permissions!

